# Contextualization Walkthrough

This distro starts with a working demo profile. Replace demo values with local
deployment values in the order below.

Run:

```bash
python3 tools/contextualize/oe_context.py doctor
python3 tools/contextualize/oe_context.py apply --profile demo --dry-run
```

## Project Identity

Surface id: `project_identity`.

Set `project_name` and `context_name` to the public-facing deployment identity.

## Environment Defaults

Surface id: `env_defaults`.

Copy `.env.example` to `.env`. Both files ship with secrets generated at
`copier copy --trust` time, so the demo stack boots without further edits.
(The post-generate task that materializes the secrets only runs when the
template is trusted — `--trust` on the initial `copier copy`, or a `y` to
the trust prompt otherwise.) Before going to production, rotate the
generated secrets in `.env` and confirm with the pre-production gate:

```bash
python3 tools/contextualize/oe_context.py doctor --prod
```

`doctor --prod` fails if `POSTGRES_PASSWORD` or `FHIRSTORE_PASSWORD` in
`.env` still match the value in `.env.example`, or if any
known-bad value (the upstream `adminADMIN!`, the literal `change-me`,
the `__GENERATED_SECRET__` sentinel) is present. The default
`doctor` (no `--prod`) only warns on unrotated demo values so the
quickstart stays a clean green.

## System Properties

Surface id: `system_properties`.

Review banner text, default nationality, phone validation rules, geographic
labels, and EQA defaults.

## Common Properties

Surface id: `common_properties`.

Set `org.openelisglobal.facility.id` and location identity values.

## Timezone

Surface id: `timezone`.

Use a valid IANA timezone, for example `UTC` or `Africa/Nairobi`.

## Analyzer Profiles

Surface id: `analyzer_profiles`.

Keep generic vendor profiles that match the deployment, then add country-specific
test-code mappings in the generated country repo.
